Multiline","inputs":{"value":"Photorealistic, cinematic, cold overcast rain light, a wuxia film set inside a downpour.\n\nCamera: medium shot from a slightly low angle, locked-off and creeping forward very slowly, keeping her near the center of frame throughout.\n\nSetting: an endless green bamboo grove, thick and thin bamboo stalks layered densely into the distance. The storm bends whole sections of the grove over in one direction and springs them back, the leaf canopy rolling like a green sea. The ground is soaked mud and standing water, hammered into white splashes and spreading ripples. Rain mist and cold moisture hang in the air, with the far bamboo fading into pale grey.\n\nSubject: a lone woman in flowing white ancient-style robes with wide sleeves and a pale cyan gauze outer layer, a sash at her waist, long black hair half tied with a ribbon trailing behind. She carries no umbrella and barely moves, standing quietly with her eyes lowered.\n\nStorm: heavy rain pours straight down, running in sheets off the bamboo leaves and stalks, bursting into fine spray on her shoulders and clothing; strong wind sweeps horizontally across the frame, throwing her wide white sleeves and hem high, the fabric snapping and billowing, the soaked fabric clinging to her frame, and her black hair and ribbon blown as one mass to one side, swinging across her cheek.\n\nFalling leaves: large numbers of dry yellow bamboo leaves and broad leaves are torn up by the wind, spinning across the foreground, skittering in sheets over the standing water, a few clinging to her white robe and wet hair.\n\nEnding: the camera creeps in to a medium close-up just in front of her, and she very slightly lifts her eyes. The rain is still falling, the wind is still blowing.\n\nSingle continuous take, no cuts."},"_meta":{"title":"Prompt"}},"453":{"class_type":"CLIPLoader","inputs":{"clip_name":"gemma4_e2b_it_int8_convrot.safetensors","type":"ltxv","device":"default"},"_meta":{"title":"CLIPLoader"}},"454":